         <h2 id="s10-9-purchases-subscriptions-revenuecat-and">9. Purchases, subscriptions, RevenueCat, and coins</h2>
-        <p>Phraseman Plus subscriptions, free trials, and other purchases made in the App are billed through the Apple App Store or Google Play, and Knowly does not receive your payment card or bank details. Purchases and gifts made on the Knowly website are paid through Stripe or PayPal, as described in section 14.</p>
+        <p>Phraseman Plus (monthly) and Ultra (yearly) subscriptions, free trials, and other purchases made in the App are billed through the Apple App Store or Google Play, and Knowly does not receive your payment card or bank details. Purchases and gifts made on the Knowly website are paid through Stripe or PayPal, as described in section 14.</p>
         <p>We use RevenueCat to verify subscriptions, entitlements, receipts, product IDs, transaction IDs, store, environment, purchase and expiry timestamps, cancellation or billing status, refund and chargeback signals, and related webhook events. RevenueCat may receive a Phraseman app user ID, Firebase/Auth ID, canonical stable ID, and attributes such as `phraseman_uid` so subscription and purchase state can be restored and matched to your account. To show whether you have access to paid features, the App checks your subscription status with RevenueCat each time it starts — including before you buy anything and before the optional choices in onboarding. For this check RevenueCat receives the app user ID described above and the technical store and device information needed to read store receipts. It is not used for advertising or analytics and is necessary to provide the App and restore purchases (performance of the App and our legitimate interests; see Legal bases).</p>
         <p>Coins are a virtual in-app balance earned through learning and rewards and spent inside the App (for example on Community Packs). We may store coin balances, grants, spending, refunds/reversals, pack purchases, seller credits, platform fees, reward grants, and audit logs in Firebase.</p>
 
