         <h2 id="s21-20-account-and-data-deletion">20. Account and data deletion</h2>
         <p>You can request deletion from inside the App where available, from the public deletion instructions at https://knowlyapps.com/legal/data-deletion/, or by emailing support.phraseman@gmail.com with subject &quot;Delete My Data&quot;.</p>
-        <p>The in-app deletion flow starts an authenticated backend deletion request. The App signs you out and clears local app data on that device immediately. A technical offline cache kept by the Firebase database library on the device is cleared the next time the App starts after the deletion. For an account signed in with Google or Apple, server-side deletion is then scheduled after a 14-day grace period, so that an accidental deletion can still be undone: if you sign in again during those 14 days, the App offers to restore the account, and accepting cancels the deletion and returns your data in full. Once the 14 days elapse, deletion runs and becomes irreversible. Where available in the app, you can also choose to delete your account immediately; in that case your data is deleted right away and cannot be restored. The backend deletion function is designed to delete or de-identify active account data controlled by Knowly, including the Firebase Auth user, users/{stable_id} data and subcollections, leaderboard/profile records, auth links, name/friend/referral indexes, Community Pack, report, reaction, poll-vote, survey, analytics, and error records linked to the stable ID; your likes, pack additions, comments and contest votes on other users' Community Packs; and local app data on the device.</p>
+        <p>The in-app deletion flow starts an authenticated backend deletion request. The App signs you out and clears local app data on that device immediately. A technical offline cache kept by the Firebase database library on the device is cleared the next time the App starts after the deletion. For an account signed in with Google or Apple, server-side deletion is then scheduled after a 14-day grace period, so that an accidental deletion can still be undone: if you sign in again during those 14 days, the App offers to restore the account, and accepting cancels the deletion and returns your data in full. Once the 14 days elapse, deletion runs and becomes irreversible. When deletion runs, we also remove every other sign-in record (Google, Apple, or email) that was linked to your account, so that signing in again with the same provider afterwards creates a new, empty account. Where available in the app, you can also choose to delete your account immediately; in that case your data is deleted right away and cannot be restored. The backend deletion function is designed to delete or de-identify active account data controlled by Knowly, including the Firebase Auth user, users/{stable_id} data and subcollections, leaderboard/profile records, auth links, name/friend/referral indexes, Community Pack, report, reaction, poll-vote, survey, analytics, and error records linked to the stable ID; your likes, pack additions, comments and contest votes on other users' Community Packs; and local app data on the device.</p>
+        <p>Community Packs you created are deleted in full, together with the likes, additions and comments that other users left on them. Likes, additions, comments and contest votes that you left under other users' packs are deleted when your account deletion runs. The like and add totals shown next to a pack are not recalculated afterwards.</p>
         <p>Friend duels are handled so that the other person's history stays intact. If you delete your account, finished duels with a friend (their result and date) and the friend's notification about that result stay in your former friend's duel history, so their own record does not change. Your account ID, nickname and avatar are removed from those records and replaced with &quot;Deleted player&quot;; they are no longer linked to you and are visible only to that friend. Open duel challenges you have not answered are deleted. In the same way, if a friend deletes their account, your finished duels with them stay in your history under &quot;Deleted player&quot;.</p>
         <p>After deletion we keep a minimal record that a deletion took place: one-way cryptographic hashes of the account identifiers (which cannot be turned back into them), the date and the reason. We keep it to demonstrate that your request was completed and to prevent abuse; it contains no profile, progress or content. While a deletion is pending we also keep the deletion request itself (account identifiers and the scheduled date) so it can run or be cancelled if you restore the account.</p>
         <p>If you use the App without signing in with Google or Apple (a guest account), deletion works the same way, except that a guest account has no sign-in method and therefore cannot be restored after you delete it. The App clears local app data on the device immediately and sends the deletion request to our servers in the background; for a guest account, server-side deletion starts as soon as our servers receive the request and confirm that no Google or Apple sign-in is linked to the account, because a guest account cannot be restored; if that cannot be confirmed at that moment, the ordinary 14-day period applies. If the request cannot reach our servers at that moment (for example, if the device is offline), the App keeps the deletion pending and sends the request again the next time it starts with a connection. If you uninstall the App before that happens, contact us as described below.</p>
